Usage: trimvol [Options] input_file output_file
Options can be abbreviated, current short name abbreviations are in parentheses
Options:
 -x  OR  -XStartAndEnd   2 ints
    Starting and ending X coordinate of region to cut out
 -y  OR  -YStartAndEnd   2 ints
    Starting and ending Y coordinate of region to cut out
 -z  OR  -ZStartAndEnd   2 ints
    Starting and ending Z coordinate of region to cut out
 -nx  OR  -XSize   Int
    Number of pixels to cut out in X, centered on the middle in X
 -ny  OR  -YSize   Int
    Number of pixels to cut out in Y, centered on the middle in Y
 -nz  OR  -ZSize   Int
    Number of slices to cut out in Z, centered on the middle in Z
 -sz  OR  -ZFindStartAndEnd   2 ints
    Scale to bytes, analyzing the given range of slices in Z
 -sx  OR  -XFindStartAndEnd   2 ints
    Starting and ending X coordinates to analyze for scaling to bytes
 -sy  OR  -YFindStartAndEnd   2 ints
    Starting and ending Y coordinates to analyze for scaling to bytes
 -c  OR  -ContrastBlackWhite   2 ints
    Contrast levels for scaling and converting to bytes
 -meansd (-me)  OR  -ScaleToMeanAndSD   2 floats
    Scale to the given mean and SD, convert to bytes by default
 -mm  OR  -IntegerMinMax   2 floats
    Scale min and max to the given values, convert to integers by default
 -mode (-mo)  OR  -ModeToOutput   Int
    Storage mode of output file; 0 for byte, 1 or 6 for integer, 2 or 12 for
    float
 -rx (-r)  OR  -RotateX
    Rotate volume by -90 degrees around X axis
 -yz  OR  -FlipYZ
    Exchange (flip) Y and Z in output volume
 -format (-fo)  OR  -FormatOfOutputFile   String
    Type of output file: MRC, TIF or TIFF, HDF (or lower case)
 -i  OR  -IndexCoordinates
    Treat as index coordinates (numbered from 0) rather than as 3dmod
    coordinates (numbered from 1, the default)
 -f  OR  -FlippedCoordinates
    Treat coordinates as coming from a volume viewed with flipping in 3dmod
 -old (-o)  OR  -OldFlippedCoordinates   Int
    Some or all Z coordinates are based on flipping with Y and Z axes swapped
 -k  OR  -KeepOrigin
    Keep origin the same in output from Newstack (legacy)
 -PID
    Print process ID
 -help (-h)  OR  -usage
    Print help output
